WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.460
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:12.940
The reading from the Sinaxadion, for October 9th, on which we commemorate,

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:24.740
our righteous forefather, Abraham, and his nephew, Lot, Abraham was born in Er of the Caldese,

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:30.140
about 1200 years before the incarnation of our Lord.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:36.900
He was descended from Shem and married to Sarah, who was childless.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:42.540
God chose Abraham to make him the Father of his people, saying,

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:48.180
go from your country, and your kindred, and your father's house,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:54.940
to the land that I will show you, and I will make of you a great nation,

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.980
and I will bless you and make your name great

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:01.940
so that you will be a blessing.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:08.660
I will bless those who bless you, and him who curses you, I will curse.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:16.420
And by you, all the families of the earth shall bless themselves.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:21.180
Abraham believed in the Word of the Lord, and without looking back,

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.780
he took his wife, Sarah, his nephew, Lot, his goods, and his servants,

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:32.420
and set off by the straight way for the land of Canaan.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:39.140
God responded to Abraham's faith by making a covenant with him and his descendants

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:46.980
that was to be everlasting, symbolized by the circumcision of all his male descendants.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:52.660
Since Sarah was barren, and both she and Abraham were very old,

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:59.140
the birth of Isaac was the first sign that God would fulfill his promise.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:04.380
So it is that Isaac prefigures the future Messiah, Christ,

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:12.180
who brings to complete perfection the promise God made to the Holy Patriarch.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:17.820
In order to test the faith of his servant, God commanded him to offer his son

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:21.540
as a burnt offering on Mount Mariah.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:27.940
Without a word of objection, Abraham saddled his donkey, cut the wood,

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:31.740
and set off with Isaac and two servants.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:37.100
When they reached Mount Mariah, where the temple of Solomon would later be built,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:45.340
the Holy Patriarch laid the wood on Isaac's back, and took the fire and the knife in his hand.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:52.100
Isaac asked where the lamb for the sacrifice was, and Abraham replied,

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:58.100
God will provide himself the lamb for a burnt offering, my son.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:07.100
Then he built an altar, bound Isaac, and laid him on it upon the wood.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:12.580
Just as he had the knife in his hand and ready to sacrifice his son,

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:19.020
the angel of the Lord called to him from heaven and held him back, saying,

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.820
do not lay your hand on the lad.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:32.060
For now I know that you fear God, seeing you that you have not withheld your only son from me.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:38.980
Abraham lifted his eyes and saw a ram caught by his horns in a thicket,

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:45.340
which he sacrificed instead of his son, and he called the name of that place,

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:49.060
on the mountain God appeared.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:54.740
The Lord then spoke again through his angel, renewing the promise that he would multiply

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:58.620
as the stars of heaven his descendants of his servants,

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:02.980
and that all nations of the earth should be blessed by them.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:08.380
Abraham died full of years, aged 175.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:14.820
He was buried in the land of Canaan, in the field he had bought for Sarah's burial.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:21.380
When Lot entered the land of Canaan with Abraham, he claimed the rich and fertile valley of the Jordan

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:24.060
and settled at Sodom.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:28.900
The people there were given over to a shameless and perverse way of life.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:34.900
The Lord's wrath was kindled against them, and he decided to destroy the city,

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:40.660
so he sent two angels to warn Lot and his family to flee, saying,

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.620
"'Flee for your life.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:47.340
Do not look back or stop anywhere in the valley.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:52.540
Flea to the hills, lest you be consumed.'"

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:59.260
The moment Lot fled, the Lord rained fire and brimstone upon Sodom and Gomorrah,

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:05.620
so as to cast all the sinners into eternal torments of hell, prepared for them.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:12.060
But Lot's wife disobeyed the Lord's commandment and looked back.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:18.980
She was straight away transformed into a pillar of salt as a lesson to us coming after.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:24.340
To follow the divine calling, without a single glance back,

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:33.230
at the world and evil ways, God has enabled us to put behind us.

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:38.630
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord, Jesus Christ our God,

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:41.870
have mercy on us and save us.
